{{also|mean time}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|mean time}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|menetime}}, equivalent to {{compound|en|mean|time}}. Adverb is by [[ellipsis]] from {{m|en||in the meantime}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|mēnʹtīm}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈmiːntaɪm/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-meantime.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[time]] spent [[waiting]] for another event; time in [[between]].
#: {{ux|en|I'll get started tomorrow but, in the '''meantime''', let's see if we can get a few more opinions.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|between-time}}, {{l|en|meanwhile}}; see also [[Thesaurus:interim]]

====Derived terms====
{{col|en
|for the mean time,for the meantime
|in mean time,in meantime
|in the mean time,in the meantime
|this mean time,this meantime
}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|meanwhile}}

