===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[during|During]] the [[interval]]; [[meanwhile]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1919|author=w:Boris Sidis|title=s:The Source and Aim of Human Progress|text='''Meantime''' Pope Urban II convoked two councils, one after another.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1934|author=w:Rex Stout|title=[[w:Fer-de-Lance (book)|''Fer-de-Lance'']]|year_published=1992|edition=[[w:Bantam Books|Bantam]] |isbn=0553278193|page=97|text=Lunch will be in twenty minutes. '''Meantime''': I have{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1951|month=May|author=J. Pelham Maitland|title=A Memorable Run by a Brighton "Terrier"|journal=Railway Magazine|page=347|text='''Meantime''', the train went on to Brighton without further incident. No small stir was caused by its arrival with No. 61 at its head, resplendent with "East London Line Special" head boards, which at once caught the eye of William Stroudley, who was observing the traffic working from his office window.}}

====Usage notes====
Usually appears sentence-initially.

